question:
(a) The table below shows the distribution of marks of 100 candidates in a JUPEB examination.
Mark range: 21-33, 31-44, 41-55, 51-66, 61-77, 71-88
Frequency: 9, 22, 25, 20, 16, 8
(i) Draw the cumulative frequency curve for the distribution;
(ii) from the curve, obtain the semi-interquartile range of the distribution;
(iii) how many students passed the examination if 50% was the pass mark?

(b) The average height of a certain age group of people is 53 inches. The standard deviation is 4 inches. If the variable is normally distributed, find the probability that the selected individual's height will be
(i) greater than 55 inches;
(ii) between 50 and 55 inches.

(b) Suppose that a pair of fair dice are to be tossed, and let the random variable X denote the sum of the points.
(i) Obtain the probability distribution for X;
(ii) find the cumulative distribution function (distribution function) F(x) for random variable X.

(c) The distribution function for a random variable X is given in the figure.
(i) find the density function f(x);
(ii) using the value of f(x), compute P(-3 < X ≤ 4).

(c) A missile is fired from Town A to another Town B 1000 m apart at an angle 50° to the horizontal.
(i) What is the initial velocity of the missile;
(ii) how long is the ball in flight before striking the ground;
(iii) what is the greatest elevation of the missile before landing. (g = 10 m/s²)
